    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d1af08ff_5c083618",
        "filename": "include/config.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 3811,
      "author": {
        "id": 1284593
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-07T20:52:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added some guidance for adjusting these terms.\n\nWe are really concerned about the minimum cell\u0027s individual state of charge.  But rather than encode a bunch of chemistry-specific knowledge about the cells, we are using imbalance and total pack state of charge (when very low) as a proxy for the weakest cell\u0027s state of charge.\n\nAnother way to think about it: CONFIG_CHARGER_MIN_BAT_PCT_IMBALANCED_POWER_ON acts to turn off the feature in case we get it wrong.  That way, the worst-case scenario is that the user has to wait just a bit longer before their system can turn on.",
      "parentUuid": "5b2648fc_689e6f34",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3811,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 3811,
        "endChar": 56
      },
